# G066 — Vending Machine

*v2. See `vending-machine.md` for prose: 4-state FSM (idle / coins-inserted /
dispensing / refunding), change-making subalgorithm, slot inventory.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Automated Snack Restocking

[restock-cycle @machines
    IN ORDER TO
        restock each machine in the fleet
        but only when the machine is in a state safe for interference

    for @m in @machines
        @inventory <- [vm[inventory-snapshot {machine: @m}]]
        @low-slots <- @inventory:slots where quantity < 2
        @low-change <- @inventory:coins where count < 10

        @m
            where
                state is "idle"
                and inserted-cents equals 0
                    (no pending customer transaction)
            IN ORDER TO
                avoid interfering with a customer mid-purchase
            || -> #skip-machine @m:id "busy"

        @order <- [warehouse[prepare-delivery
                              {machine-id: @m:id,
                               products: @low-slots:slot-ids,
                               coins: @low-change:denoms}]]
        [warehouse[dispatch {order: @order}]]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[vm
    new
    add-slot            {slot}
    load-change         {denom, count}
    insert-coin         {denom}                    ;; || not-in-idle-or-coins-inserted
    select              {slot-id}                  ;; (product, change) || insufficient-funds, out-of-stock
    refund                                          ;; always legal
    inventory-snapshot  {machine}
    state               {machine}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: FSM transitions as `where`-gated

[vm[insert-coin {machine: @m, denom: @d}
    where state is "idle" or "coins-inserted"
        (otherwise the coin is refused and the inserted amount does not change)
]

[vm[select {machine: @m, slot-id: @slot}
    where
        state is "coins-inserted"
        and inserted-cents at least the slot's price
        and the slot has at least one unit in stock
    IN ORDER TO
        transition to "dispensing" atomically
        and compute change (or resist with insufficient-change)
]

---

## Change-making as sub-algorithm

[vm[make-change {amount: @cents, coins: @inventory:coins}
    where
        result is a multiset of coins summing to @cents
        using the greedy algorithm over available denominations
        || resists with "cannot-make-exact-change"
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @m <- [vm[new]]
    [vm[add-slot {slot: {id: "A1", product: "Chips", price-cents: 150, quantity: 5}}]]
    [vm[add-slot {slot: {id: "B2", product: "Cola",  price-cents: 125, quantity: 3}}]]
    [vm[load-change {denom: 25, count: 10}]]
    [vm[load-change {denom: 100, count: 5}]]

    -> [vm[state {machine: @m}]]    ;; -> "idle"

    [vm[insert-coin {machine: @m, denom: 100}]]
    [vm[insert-coin {machine: @m, denom: 100}]]
    -> [vm[state {machine: @m}]]    ;; -> "coins-inserted"

    @(product, change) <- [vm[select {machine: @m, slot-id: "A1"}]]
    -> @product:product               ;; -> "Chips"
    -> @change                         ;; -> multiset summing to 50 cents
]
